menu "BLUECHERRY Configuration"

    config BLUECHERRY_AUTO_SYNC_SEC
        int "Auto Sync Interval (seconds)"
        default 10
        range 1 3600
        help
            Set the interval in seconds for automatic synchronization when no messages are published.
            Minimum is 1 second, maximum is 3600 seconds (1 hour).

    config BLUECHERRY_SYNC_TASK_STACK_SIZE
        int "Synchronisation Task Stack Size (bytes)"
        default 8192
        range 4096 32768
        help
            Stack for the background synchronisation task, which runs every network operation
            this library performs. The deepest path is zero-touch provisioning: a DTLS
            handshake with certificate chain verification, then CBOR exchanges holding up to
            2.8 kB of buffers in nested frames, then SECP256R1 key generation. 4096 is not
            enough for that and overflows. Lower it only if you never use ZTP.

    config BLUECHERRY_PUBLISH_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "Publish Buffer Size (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 256 262144
        help
            Size of the buffer holding messages that are waiting to be published, used only
            when the application passes no buffer of its own to bluecherry_init. Each queued
            message costs its payload plus 9 bytes; a message that does not fit in the buffer
            can never be queued at all. Pass a buffer to bluecherry_init to place this in
            PSRAM or in memory the application reserved itself.

endmenu
